description:
Exploration question: Which `getUser` does each file in `src/billing/` call, and what does that one do?

Files read (every line is numbered as `line | code`; this is everything that has been read):

`src/db/users.ts`
```
1 | import { db } from "../db";
2 | 
3 | export async function getUser(id: string): Promise<User> {
4 |   return db.one("SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?", [id]);
5 | }
```

`src/api/users.ts`
```
1 | import { userService } from "./clients";
2 | 
3 | export async function getUser(id: string): Promise<UserProfile> {
4 |   const res = await userService.get(`/users/${id}`);
5 |   return res.json();
6 | }
```

`src/billing/invoice.ts`
```
1 | import { getUser } from "../db/users";
2 | 
3 | export async function buildInvoice(userId: string, cents: number) {
4 |   const user = await getUser(userId);
5 |   return { to: user.email, cents };
6 | }
```

`src/billing/notify.ts`
```
1 | import { getUser } from "../api/users";
2 | 
3 | export async function notifyOverdue(userId: string) {
4 |   const profile = await getUser(userId);
5 |   await sendEmail(profile.email, "Your invoice is overdue");
6 | }
```
